# Known-intentional doc references that deliberately do not resolve in-repo.
# check_doc_refs.rb skips every line listed here.
#
# Format: one backticked reference per line, exactly as the doc writes it
# (`Foo::Bar`, no backticks, no trailing text). Blank lines and lines starting
# with `#` are ignored. Keep entries grouped under a `# ---` comment that says WHY
# (an illustrative example class in a pattern doc, a removed name a decision
# records on purpose, a gem class named by a short alias). Anything not listed
# here that fails the check is real drift: fix the doc or the code instead.
# `ruby .claude/scripts/documentation/check_doc_refs.rb --unused` lists entries
# no doc names any more, so delete those.

# --- an illustrative host policy: the docs show the conventional shape of a
# concrete policy's nested scope; the class is a host's, never defined in the
# gem (the spec builds an anonymous policy class)
WidgetPolicy::Scope
